mod:list_ptr_through_wrapper;
// A POINTER PARAMETER INSIDE AN OPTIONAL OR A `Result` IS ASKED AS THE POINTER, AT EVERY LEVEL (DEF-601, landing 177d2b3). A pointer parameter handed to a call is the
// address of its pointee (DEF-584), and a value read out of a parameter is asked by the type it was read as (DEF-590). An unwrap (`??!`, `??`, `?!`, `?|`, `relay`)
// yields the wrapper's one value and no reader marks it, so the parameter's ref kept the wrapper's type, an Optional or a `Result`, which is no pointer, and
// nothing held the pointee: `int64->:e = raw fp(o ??! E5); discard(raw growh(o ??! E5)); pass <-e;` read freed heap on main and on every build before this row.
// Now `passed_pointee` peels every wrapper (`H->?`, `Result<H->>`, `Result<H->?>`, …) to what it holds and asks that. Each module is one cell; each fault cell takes
// `e = raw fp(<the pointer>)`, grows the same `List` and reads `e`. `…p` is a cell's plain-pointer twin, `…l` its local twin (the wrapper a local over a local `H`).
// THE OPTIONAL (`zo`, `zn`, `zf1`, `zk1`, `zk2`): `zo1d`, `zo1k`, `zo1r` an Optional parameter unwrapped by `??!`, the growth direct, through an identity's held result
// and through an identity in the argument; `zo2d`, `zo2k`, `zo2r` an Optional member of a pointer parameter; `zo3` to `zo8` an Optional LOCAL, refused before this
// row (the yardstick). `zn1`, `zn1b`, `zn37` `??` with a local default; `zn2` the unwrap held; `zn3` a by-value struct's member; `zn4` `?.`; `zn5` an Optional local
// of a plain parameter; `zn6` an array of Optionals; `zn7` an aggregate holder; `zn8` one expression; `zn9`, `zn9s` a taker's `Result` unwrapped; `zn10` the callee
// unwraps the take; `zn13`, `zn14` an identity's result and a copy held as Optionals; `zn19`, `zn19q`, `zn28` an Optional result of a taker; `zn23`, `zn24` the
// address and the receiver through an unwrap; `zn25` the growth written in the caller; `zn26`, `zn26l`, `zn27` an Optional holder; `zn39` a `Result<H->>` parameter;
// `zn11p`, `zn32p` a callee that grows through its plain parameter. `zf1` a `for` binding over an array of Optionals; `zk1`, `zk2` a `pick` binding.
// THE `Result` (`zr`, `zf2`, `zk3`): `zr1` `?!`; `zr2`, `zr2b`, `zr2d` `?|`; `zr3` `relay`; `zr4`, `zr5` `.value` behind an `is_error` test (a member read, refused before);
// `zr10`, `zr10k`, `zr10r` a `Result` member of a pointer parameter; `zr11` of a by-value struct; `zr12` an array of `Result`s; `zr13` the callee unwraps the take;
// `zr14`, `zr14s` a `Result` result of a taker; `zr15` a copy; `zr16` a local `Result` of a plain parameter; `zr17` an identity's result held; `zr18` the receiver;
// `zr19` the growth written in the caller; `zr20` the unwrap held; `zr21` an aggregate holder; `zr22` one expression; `zr23` a `Result` holder; `zr24` the address.
// A WRAPPER IN A WRAPPER (`zw`, `zd`): `zw1` `Result<H->?>`; `zw2` `Result<H->>?`; `zw3` `Result<Result<H->>>`; `zw4` an Optional member read by `?.` through an Optional pointer;
// `zw5` to `zw7` a by-value struct or array inside a wrapper; `zw8` three wrappers; `zw9` handed whole to a callee; `zw10` a member of a pointer parameter; `zw11` an array's element;
// `zd4r`, `zd64r` 4 and 64 levels of `Result` over `H->`, and `zd4a`, `zd64a` of `Result<…?>` alternating: the asker's loop takes one step per level and ends at the pointer.
// SIX RIGHT PROGRAMS ARE REFUSED HERE, THE ROW'S NAMED PRICES (`…_price`), each in line with its plain twin and with its local twin. `zn34`, `zr34`, `zw13`: a struct
// holds the wrapper beside another pointer, the growth goes through the wrapper and the other pointer is read. `zn36`, `zr36`, `zw14`: a callee returns the address of
// the pointee's scalar member, held across the growth. Their plain-pointer twins `zn34p`, `zn36p` (`…_price584`) are refused since DEF-584, and so is `zn40p` (a callee
// writes a scalar through a copy of its pointer parameter while an element pointer is held). Every local twin (`…_local_price575`) is refused since DEF-575.
mod:zd4a_nest = {
error:E5_zd4a_nest;
struct:K = { int64:k; };
struct:H = { List<int64>:l; int64:k; K:kk; };
struct:H2 = { H:inner; int64:z; };
struct:HP = { H->:lp; int64:z; };
struct:W = { H->:hp; int64:z; };
struct:S = { int64:a; int64:b; };
struct:PE = { int64->:p; int64:z; };
enum:EK = { A(int64->); Z; };
func:rdk = int64(EK:e) never fails { int64:v = 0i64; pick (e) { (EK.A(q)) { v = <-q; }, (EK.Z) { v = 0i64; } } pass v; };
func:mk = List<int64>() never fails { List<int64>:l = raw list_init::<int64>(1i64); drop list_push(@l, 1i64); pass l; };
